From: Matthew Feickert <matthew.feickert@cern.ch>
Subject: [PATCH] Link against the conda-forge nng and Mbed TLS on Windows

Upstream's src/Makevars.ucrt always compiles the bundled NNG and Mbed TLS
sources into nanonext.dll. conda-forge prefers its shared nng and mbedtls
packages over bundled copies, so compile only the package's own sources and
link against the import libraries in %LIBRARY_PREFIX% (R_HOME is
%PREFIX%/Lib/R). NNG_STATIC_LIB is dropped so that nng.h declares the
functions as dllimport.
---
--- a/src/Makevars.ucrt
+++ b/src/Makevars.ucrt
@@ -7,5 +7,5 @@
 # PKG_CFLAGS carries $(C_VISIBILITY) to hide the bundled nng_*/mbedtls_* symbols.
-PKG_CPPFLAGS = -Inng/include -Imbedtls/include -DNNG_STATIC_LIB
+PKG_CPPFLAGS = -I$(R_HOME)/../../Library/include
 PKG_CFLAGS = $(C_VISIBILITY)
-PKG_LIBS = -lws2_32 -lmswsock -ladvapi32 -lbcrypt -liphlpapi
+PKG_LIBS = -L$(R_HOME)/../../Library/lib -lnng -lmbedtls -lmbedx509 -lmbedcrypto -lws2_32 -lmswsock -ladvapi32 -lbcrypt -liphlpapi
 
@@ -21,3 +21,3 @@
 
-OBJECTS = $(P_OBJECTS) $(NNG_OBJECTS) $(MBEDTLS_OBJECTS)
+OBJECTS = $(P_OBJECTS)
 
